{% comment %}
  Renders the brand lockup — the logo image, or the square mark beside the
  wordmark. Shared by the header and the footer so the two cannot drift.

  Emits the inner content only; the caller supplies the wrapping <a> (or
  heading) and owns the presentation. Each section styles .--logo-mark and
  .--header-logo-text in its own scoped block, the same way every section here
  restyles the shared element classes it uses.

  The mark is the demo store's measurement motif: a bordered square with a
  small accent square notched into its top-right corner. Its colour comes from
  --mark-accent on the section container.

  Accepts:
  - logo:      {Object} image; used alone when set
  - text:      {String} wordmark; defaults to the shop name
  - show_mark: {Boolean} draw the square mark beside the wordmark
  - width:     {Number} rendered logo width in px, for the sizes attribute

  Usage:
  {% render 'custom-brand-lockup', logo: section.settings.logo, text: 'Amaze' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign wordmark = text | default: shop.name
  assign logo_w = width | default: 130
-%}

{%- if logo != blank -%}
  {{
    logo
    | image_url: width: 600
    | image_tag:
      class: '--header-logo-image',
      widths: '120, 180, 240, 360, 480, 600',
      sizes: logo_w | append: 'px',
      loading: 'eager',
      alt: shop.name
  }}
{%- else -%}
  {%- if show_mark -%}
    <span class="--logo-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- endif -%}
  <span class="--header-logo-text">{{ wordmark }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
